        "Pattern-exploiting training (PET; \\citealp{schick2021exploiting,schick2021small}) entails formatting train and test examples as cloze-style prompts, where the label is generally one word. Here, a language model can see the inputs and the embeddings of the output classes during tuning and prediction, though unlike our approach, there is no domain-general training step. Prompt tuning \\citep{lester2021power,gao2021lmbff} improves PET by automatically optimizing the prompt design. Our approach is even more widely applicable in that we give the model concatenated utterances and labels and allow it to transduce to variable-length label sequences, rather than reformatting the evaluation data into a cloze format where the label must be one word/token.\n",
