            "\\textbf{Few-shot text classification} entails performing classification after training or tuning a model on only a few examples from the training split of an evaluation set. Recent approaches to this include (Ro)BERT(a)-based \\citep{topv2} and especially XLNet-based \\citep{yang2020xlnet} classifiers, prototypical networks \\citep{snell2017prototypical}, dynamic memory induction networks \\citep{geng2020dynamic}, and generative classification (discussion follows).\n",
