            "LM-BFF \\citep{gao2021lmbff} is a prompt-tuning-based model for few-shot text classification. It uses automatically generated and optimized prompts (from T5) to perform generative classification (with RoBERTa) by predicting a masked token after the input. It achieves SOTA scores on few-shot binary/trinary sentiment classification and NLI tasks. We employ the best-performing \\emph{prompt-tuning with demonstrations} approach, adapting it for IC by reducing the intent labels to single words.\n",
