            "During fine-tuning, we use init.\\ LR $5\\times 10^{-4}$ and batch size $1$.\\footnote{We use a small batch size due to the small size of the $1$-shot splits. We do not observe significant performance differences when using batch size 2 or 4.} We tune over the number of fine-tuning epochs $\\in [1,16]$ for the largest few-shot split, typically finding $2$ epochs to be best. Once we have the best setting for the largest split, we double the number of tuning epochs for each halving of the split size such that the number of tuning steps is similar for all split sizes. All other hyperparameters are huggingface defaults.\n",
